s3
==

The s3 module of the Tryton application platform.

Installing
----------

See INSTALL

ClamAV
------

Set ``clamd`` in the ``[s3]`` section to the Unix socket of clamd, or to its
``host:port`` address. For example::

    [s3]
    clamd = /run/clamav/clamd.ctl
    # clamd = 127.0.0.1:3310

``clamd_timeout`` defaults to 30 seconds.
If ``clamd`` is not set, ClamAV scanning is disabled.
If clamd is unavailable or times out, the user receives a notification and
the file operation continues without an antivirus result.

The local cache access time is updated at most once every five minutes per
file to reduce filesystem metadata writes.

Users in the ``Antivirus Malware Warning`` group receive a warning when
malware is found. After confirming it, they may repeat the operation; other
users receive an error and cannot continue.


